# R6 (ai/type-core-calculus.typ): two refinements of one stored value. Both
# would return the same dict, at two types, and writing a string through d
# would reach p's float.
"{\"age\": 1.5}" parseJson j!
@j tryAs {age: float} ? p!
@j tryAs {str: float | str} ? d!
@d "age" "x" set drop
@p :age? 1.0 + str wl
